apple's iphone event just happened  yesterday and they finally unveiled  their iphone 12 lineup so in this video  i'm gonna wrap up all of the new  features into just a few minutes  while comparing them to the previous  iphone 11  with the goal of helping you decide if  it's worth upgrading to the iphone 12  if you already have the iphone 11 the  10r  the 8 the 7 the 6 or any other iphone  now before we get started i want to  mention that i already created a video  specifically for the iphone 12 pro  models  so if you're interested in that be sure  to watch that video after this one is  over  first things first the iphone 12 gets  the brand new design  with flat aluminum edges on the sides  which i think looks  incredibly clean just like we got on the  modern ipad pro  but what makes it even better is that  the thickness of the iphone 12 went down  to 7.4 millimeters  compared to 8.3 on the iphone 11 so it's  gonna feel  super nice especially since it's now 16  percent lighter  164 grams compared to 194 grams on the  11.  and because of the flat sides the glass  on the front is no longer  curved which allowed apple to make the  bezels thinner  while keeping the same 6.1 inch display  size  which leads to a 15 smaller and more  compact phone  and by the way the thinner bezels make  the notch look smaller  while it physically isn't so keep that  in mind now i do want to mention that  for the first time ever  there's also the new iphone 12 mini  which comes with a 5.4 inch display  making it much smaller and lighter being  a great choice for kids  or people with smaller hands but keep in  mind that the battery life  isn't going to be as good but other than  the size the mini is  literally identical to the regular 12 in  terms of the features and the specs  so everything that i'm gonna say about  the iphone 12 for the rest of this video  also applies to the mini except for the  unfortunate fact  that the mini is not going to be  shipping until next month  starting at 699 another interesting  difference is that the camera bump  on the back is actually larger compared  to the one on the iphone 11  and as far as the color options for the  iphone 12 yellow is going away  while there is a new shade of green and  a new blue color  to replace the purple on the iphone 11  and while they still have product red  it looks quite a bit lighter than the  iphone 11 version  now perhaps the most shocking feature is  the display the iphone 12 now gets the  same  exact super retina xdr oled display  as the pro models which is a massive  upgrade  from the iphone 11 which used an lcd  display  this means the iphone 12 gets 1200 nits  of peak brightness while viewing hdr  content  it gets much more contrast much better  colors  and a huge boost in pixels per inch  at 460 just like the pro model  the only downside is that the iphone 12  maxes out at 625 nits in typical use  compared to 800 nits on the iphone 12  pro models  apple has now upgraded the front glass  using a new ceramic substrate technology  giving it four times better drop  protection according to apple  and a huge upgrade is water resistance  ip68 at 6 meters for up to 30 minutes  compared to only 2 meters  on the iphone 11. now a pretty huge new  feature that apple focused a lot on  during the event  is 5g support but we totally  weren't expecting the regular iphone 12  to also support millimeter wave 5g  specifically for us customers  so compared to the iphone 11 you're  getting sub 65g  millimeter wave 5g and faster regular  lte speeds  up to 2 gigabits per second with 4x4  mimo  compared to 1 gigabit per second with  2x2 mimo on the iphone 11.  apple also released the new smart data  mode which automatically switches to lte  when you don't need 5g speed so that  helps keep the rated battery life the  same as the iphone 11  which is very surprising considering the  fact that the 12 got smaller  and thinner the iphone 12 also gets the  new super efficient  5 nanometer a14 bionic chip which is  quite a bit faster  in basically every single way so if you  want to see the full comparison with  benchmarks and performance differences  subscribe right now so you don't miss  out now before i get into the camera  differences  i want to touch on a feature that i'm  really excited for  magsafe apple has basically built  magnets into the wireless charging coil  inside of the iphone itself so the brand  new  super compact magsafe wireless charger  magnetically snaps onto the back of the  iphone  so you can actually use it while it's  wirelessly charging  at a much faster 15 watts compared to  7.5 watts  using qi chargers like the iphone 11 is  limited to  but what makes it even more special is  the new mac safe accessories  like the wallet which can hold onto the  back of a naked iphone 12  with nothing but the built-in magnets  there's also a lineup of new cases  which have magnets built into the case  itself as well so they're easier to put  on and  take off and you can even add the wallet  on top of the case  thanks to the magnets apple also has a  couple of extra magsafe accessories  coming in the future  like the magsafe duo charger a magnetic  car mount and a multi-charging dock from  belkin  and apple has already confirmed that  third-party companies are beginning  to make accessories like pop socket  which will use the magnets in creative  ways  now i personally think that this is  going to be a bigger deal  than most people are making it out to be  and we just have to wait and see what  accessory makers  will come up with in the near future now  let's finally get  into the cameras and while you might not  think there's that big of a difference  since we get the same three cameras as  before there actually  are some interesting upgrades first off  i want to mention that the a14 chip's  extra performance  impacts every camera feature especially  the neural engine  which is now twice as fast and it also  comes with a new image signal processor  as well  so keep that in mind the hardware on the  ultrawide camera  is basically unchanged but the wide  camera is getting some new upgrades  first off it has a faster f 1.6 aperture  compared to f 1.8 on the 11  so it lets in more light and it gets a  new seven element lens  compared to the old one with six  elements so these changes help the  iphone 12's  wide camera get 27 percent better low  light performance  not only that but apple mentioned that  the optical image stabilization is now  up to five times faster than before  so your video footage should be more  stable and your photos will turn out  sharp  more often than before what's really  exciting is that we now finally have  night mode on all of the cameras  including  the selfie camera while the iphone 11  only gets it on the main one  and it's the exact same story for  apple's deep fusion feature  and we'll be testing out exactly how  much better those deep fusion selfies  are going to look  compared to the iphone 11 so if you're  not already subscribed  do so right now and by the way thank you  guys for helping us  finally reach 400 000 subscribers so  let's go for 500k  the iphone 12 also gets the third  generation of smart hdr  with scene detection so you're not only  getting improved dynamic range  but it now looks at and adjusts various  parts of the scene  instead of just your face in the  background like it did on the iphone 11  in terms of video recording we now get a  new night mode  time lapse feature and you can now  record in the new  dolby vision hdr mode at up to 30 frames  per second  compared to 60 fps on the pro models but  we're not really sure how big of a deal  this will be for most people  alright so there you guys go those are  all the changes and new features  compared to last year's iphone 11  so now let's get into if it's actually  worth upgrading  first off if you have the iphone 10r or  older  like the iphone 6 7 or the 8  then i would 100 recommend upgrading  because the value of the iphone 12 is  just insane for  the price and the camera quality is so  much better than even the iphone 10r  and people who love smaller iphones can  now get the mini  which gets identical features and specs  as the iphone 12.  but by far the most difficult upgrade  decision  is if you already have the iphone 11 so  let's get into the features that will  actually matter  in the real world while you might not  care about 5g  it could actually make a huge difference  in day-to-day use  the best 4g lte speed we've ever got on  the iphone 11 pro max  using t-mobile has been around 59  megabits per second  even with full bars and very recently  speed tests have been released showing  mid band 5g on t-mobile's network  using the iphone 12 reaching speeds of  up to 621 megabits per second  and that's not even sub 65g on top of  that  i do want to remind you that regular lte  is getting twice as fast compared to the  iphone 11  so there's a very good chance that the  iphone 12 will greatly  improve cellular service across the  board  making it much better for people who are  having issues right now  another huge reason to upgrade from the  iphone 11 to the 12  is of course the new design which is  most likely going to stay  this way for the next few years and i  think the new max save feature is going  to be a huge hit  once more accessories become available  by far  the biggest change is in the displays  you're going from an lcd panel  with low resolution to quite literally  the same oled panel that you get on the  iphone 12 pro  so display quality is getting a huge  upgrade of course  you've now got the new a14 chip and  we're gonna have to see how fast that  really is  and the cameras should be a good  improvement across the board  especially since you can now take night  mode shots with any of the cameras  the only real downside this year is that  you don't get a charger  or earpods in the box and since the  iphone 12 now comes with the usbc  to lightning cable people with older 5  watt charging bricks  will either have to buy a new one from  apple or buy a wireless charger  thankfully anker's new 20 watt fast  charger is currently on sale for 16  on amazon if you use the coupon so it's  perfect for the iphone 12  and i'm gonna leave links down in the  description below to that sale  but here is my final piece of advice on  if you should upgrade to the iphone 12.  in my opinion there is a much bigger  difference  going from the iphone 11 to the 12  compared to last year  when we went from the 10r to the 11. and  frankly  i'm shocked at how much value apple  packed into the 12  compared to the pro which only gets a  couple of extra features  like the telephoto lens so in my opinion  the 6.1 inch iphone 12 is the star of  the show  and i think a ton of people are going to  be upgrading from older iphones  if this video was helpful go ahead and  tap the like button  and click the circle above to subscribe  for our hands-on full comparison videos  like our unbiased camera comparison and  if you're thinking about upgrading to  the iphone 12  pro models check out that video right  over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one

